# Yield and lifetime

`Task.Yield()` is load-bearing. Measured query times dropped after adding it. Do not remove it, "optimize it out," or recommend removing it as a hot-path win.

Do not make services singletons by default, and do not recommend that as a performance fix. Scoped/transient registrations stay unless the user asks to change them. Same reason: forcing singleton lifetime made things worse.

Forbidden:
- deleting or "simplifying away" existing `await Task.Yield()`
- suggesting Yield is wasted work on cache hits
- rewriting a scoped/transient service to singleton (or hosted-singleton) without being asked
